1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,116
Twelve people asleep behind frosted glass, one switch,

2
00:00:03,566 --> 00:00:05,443
and a note that says don't.

3
00:00:07,243 --> 00:00:09,706
Two of my crew are standing in front of it,

4
00:00:10,156 --> 00:00:13,600
and whichever button they press, the ship gets a different quest.

5
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:17,233
This is the checkpoint for the first half of the class.

6
00:00:17,683 --> 00:00:22,199
You'll plan one away scene on paper, type it, check it, and play it.

7
00:00:23,399 --> 00:00:25,501
Before any rooms, three sentences.

8
00:00:26,401 --> 00:00:28,218
The question the scene asks.

9
00:00:28,668 --> 00:00:32,972
Why is this hulk drifting, with nobody at the controls?

10
00:00:33,872 --> 00:00:36,379
The answer, which the party finds in pieces.

11
00:00:36,829 --> 00:00:40,649
Her crew put themselves to sleep, to wait for help that never came.

12
00:00:41,549 --> 00:00:44,206
And the choice they make at the end.

13
00:00:44,656 --> 00:00:47,529
Wake them now, or leave them and fetch a doctor.

14
00:00:49,329 --> 00:00:51,584
The pieces of the answer become your readings,

15
00:00:52,034 --> 00:00:54,787
and the choice becomes your two endings.

16
00:00:55,687 --> 00:00:57,858
If you can't write the third sentence,

17
00:00:58,308 --> 00:01:00,338
you have a tour, and not a scene.

18
00:01:01,538 --> 00:01:04,791
Next, how much of everything. Six places.

19
00:01:05,241 --> 00:01:08,003
Three readings, one for each job on my roster.

20
00:01:08,453 --> 00:01:10,576
One reading for a skill, and one check.

21
00:01:11,026 --> 00:01:14,156
Five facts in all, and a door that asks for three.

22
00:01:15,956 --> 00:01:18,551
Then I draw it, with one room in the middle,

23
00:01:19,001 --> 00:01:21,889
and every other place leads back to that room.

24
00:01:22,789 --> 00:01:25,525
The way home goes in the room they arrive in,

25
00:01:25,975 --> 00:01:28,120
and at each ending, and nowhere else.

26
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:31,143
This is the table that saves you.

27
00:01:32,043 --> 00:01:34,640
For every fact I write where it is, who's offered it,

28
00:01:35,090 --> 00:01:36,819
and whether it's sure.

29
00:01:38,619 --> 00:01:41,314
A fact is sure when every party can get it.

30
00:01:42,214 --> 00:01:44,632
A reading for a job on my roster is sure,

31
00:01:45,082 --> 00:01:48,357
because when that person stays home, somebody covers.

32
00:01:49,257 --> 00:01:51,267
A reading for a skill isn't,

33
00:01:51,717 --> 00:01:54,146
and neither is anything behind a roll.

34
00:01:55,946 --> 00:01:57,398
I have three sure facts.

35
00:01:57,848 --> 00:02:00,309
So my door may ask for three, and no more.

36
00:02:01,509 --> 00:02:02,751
This is where it's going:

37
00:02:03,201 --> 00:02:07,593
the spine on the chief's handheld, with the captain's hatch open at last.

38
00:02:09,393 --> 00:02:14,179
Now I type, in layers, and I run lint after each one. Places first,

39
00:02:14,629 --> 00:02:17,369
and I've torn out my practice rooms to make space.

40
00:02:18,269 --> 00:02:20,209
Lint warns about two signals,

41
00:02:20,659 --> 00:02:25,966
and it's right, because the rooms that sent them are gone. Then the readings. Then the check.

42
00:02:26,416 --> 00:02:32,067
Then the door, with a line that tells an early party why it's shut. Then the endings.

43
00:02:32,517 --> 00:02:35,343
Each ending is a quest the ship doesn't have yet,

44
00:02:35,793 --> 00:02:38,994
a choice that starts it, with the new word accepts,

45
00:02:39,444 --> 00:02:41,558
and a last room with one way out.

46
00:02:42,458 --> 00:02:45,597
The crew reads an ending's quest the moment they choose,

47
00:02:46,047 --> 00:02:48,152
so each one gets a short page.

48
00:02:49,052 --> 00:02:51,069
Here they are in the Quest Log:

49
00:02:51,519 --> 00:02:53,605
an hourglass on the first one,

50
00:02:54,055 --> 00:02:56,358
and a picture of the station on the other.

51
00:02:58,158 --> 00:02:59,329
Then the two stories.

52
00:02:59,779 --> 00:03:00,837
And lint is clean.

53
00:03:02,037 --> 00:03:04,221
The ship's quest gets a new page too.

54
00:03:05,121 --> 00:03:08,094
Here it is in the Quest Log on Helm:

55
00:03:08,544 --> 00:03:12,349
a table of what the station knows before anybody boards.

56
00:03:14,149 --> 00:03:16,406
And one change to how it ends.

57
00:03:17,306 --> 00:03:20,576
Last time, it waited for the surgeon's story to finish.

58
00:03:21,026 --> 00:03:24,267
But a story is handed to nobody when its person stays home,

59
00:03:24,717 --> 00:03:27,573
so a short crew could never complete it.

60
00:03:29,373 --> 00:03:31,761
Now it waits for the reading's own signal.

61
00:03:32,661 --> 00:03:36,681
The surgeon's press finishes her story and the ship's quest together,

62
00:03:37,131 --> 00:03:40,821
and when she's not there, the covered reading still finishes the ship's.

63
00:03:42,021 --> 00:03:44,917
Lint has passed, and lint checks your spelling.

64
00:03:45,367 --> 00:03:46,959
It doesn't walk through your rooms.

65
00:03:47,859 --> 00:03:49,516
So I do, with a pencil.

66
00:03:51,316 --> 00:03:54,473
One: every room has a way out with no condition.

67
00:03:55,373 --> 00:03:57,993
Two: every room has a way in.

68
00:03:58,893 --> 00:04:02,340
Three: the door asks for no more than the sure facts,

69
00:04:02,790 --> 00:04:04,880
and every fact has its own name.

70
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:08,145
Four is the big one.

71
00:04:08,595 --> 00:04:12,526
I cross out everything that needs a skill or a roll,

72
00:04:12,976 --> 00:04:15,909
and with what's left I walk to each ending.

73
00:04:16,809 --> 00:04:18,930
If I can, every crew can.

74
00:04:20,730 --> 00:04:23,987
Five: each story's reading belongs to its person,

75
00:04:24,437 --> 00:04:26,998
and each ending's quest starts hidden.

76
00:04:28,198 --> 00:04:31,261
Then I play it three times, with a watch beside me.

77
00:04:32,161 --> 00:04:33,933
Alone, I'm the chief,

78
00:04:34,383 --> 00:04:37,874
and two readings come to me marked as covering.

79
00:04:38,774 --> 00:04:41,731
Sixteen presses, and I'm home with an ending.

80
00:04:43,531 --> 00:04:46,504
With the doctor aboard too, the menus differ.

81
00:04:46,954 --> 00:04:50,329
In the hold, only she is offered the scanner's sweep.

82
00:04:51,229 --> 00:04:53,557
With all three aboard, nothing is covered,

83
00:04:54,007 --> 00:04:56,125
and reading it all takes twenty.

84
00:04:57,925 --> 00:04:59,718
And once, I walk away.

85
00:05:00,169 --> 00:05:01,585
One press in the airlock,

86
00:05:02,035 --> 00:05:05,669
and the visit is over for everybody, with nothing finished.

87
00:05:06,569 --> 00:05:08,862
That's why the way home is where it is.

88
00:05:10,062 --> 00:05:11,009
Now write your own.

89
00:05:11,909 --> 00:05:16,287
Three sentences, a beat sheet, a drawing, a facts table,

90
00:05:16,737 --> 00:05:17,919
and then the typing.

91
00:05:18,819 --> 00:05:19,928
Do the five checks,

92
00:05:20,378 --> 00:05:26,213
and break it three times on purpose, to see lint say clean when the scene is wrong.

93
00:05:28,013 --> 00:05:30,154
Then play it with everyone you can find,

94
00:05:30,604 --> 00:05:32,660
and write down how long it took.
